{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt source-only completion of the URL reputation feature under the [published Stage 1 design](notes/2026-08-31-url-reputation-stage-1-decisions.md@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:1), corrected readiness report 920e631c and the attached remaining-delivery.md handoff. This is an ordinary Hugh decision for the remaining work, not reliance on the historical Checker relay as a Hugh ratification.\n\n1. First deliver a small, independently reviewed repair of the confirmed host-binding defect in [the normalizer](tailapps/url-reputation/folds/normalize.jsonata@e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c:19), including tests and descriptions affected by that correction. Preserve the exact locally observed URL and legitimate host/port forms; reject a supplied host that differs from the actual authority host. The report's suggested parsing sketch is not adopted as an implementation algorithm: bracketed IPv6 and malformed authority cases also need explicit treatment. Builder may take this bounded repair at a safe I7 checkpoint and must preserve the full #4043 commitment.\n2. Then finish Stage 3 and Stage 4 as one remaining feature-delivery assignment to Builder, queued after the full I7 Stage 1 delivery and the already-promised Kiro assessment #4055. Stage 4 remains part of that request's conditions, with the normalizer repair's landed publication as an implementation prerequisite.\n3. Keep url-reputation opt-in. The catalog should accurately describe all embedded bundles; it does not require changing the setup default or activating a resident.\n4. Ship exact, fixture-backed capture profiles and truthful missing-coverage reporting. Codex non-managed hook definitions require explicit operator trust; hosted WebSearch is outside local hooks. Claude WebSearch support requires a real compatibility fixture and successful-result semantics; unsupported shapes stay explicit. Do not install or trust hooks during this source delivery.\n5. Preserve the existing provider eligibility, environment-only credential, mandatory exclusions/scrubbing and retention/reset contract. The handoff makes Safe Browsing expression matching and provider TTL reuse explicit; clean Web Risk Lookup responses without expiry use bounded local fallback policy. Keep one selected eligible provider, no automatic fallback and no new cache/database. Refresh the Web Risk documentation link.\n6. No actual provider calls, credentials, scheduler, resident installation/restart, activation/reset, runtime/schema extension or historical replay is authorized here. Source implementation needs separate exact-head artifacts, independent review, ratified approval, sealed merge, push, CI and owned cleanup. A source-only loopback/fake-provider proof is not evidence of real capture or live provider operation.\n\nThe cited note and normalizer bytes match current main e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c. Their live published bases carry ordinary inherited staleness from historical workflow closures; that history is acknowledged and the current source/accepted readiness evidence reconciles the planned conditions. Subsequent implementation must revalidate current bases rather than claim the staleness disappeared.","body":{"head":"e3ad5f920d63274ac0998903e0399e413f9f848c","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:6ba68c0c51ddf5e5e8672e6f8894d500ce9dfcdb, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:920e631c034dd56e18097fbe1a43da8c841f5e92, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:bf865548336fa179fe72d02d5ec51db52453a5ba stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:4472b3ba65a898d310f6225632b8a5528fbf437a, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:6c172daedfcbd0033a345a0ff0562c0988dae142, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:741734abdb11839feee6121232d3483dad337bc1, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:785b